# Release Process — TelegramAutoDownload

## MANDATORY: Every release MUST include both files

Every `gh release create` or `gh release upload` command **must** include:

1. `TelegramAutoDownload_vX.X.X_Setup.exe` — Inno Setup installer (for installed users + new installs)
2. `TelegramAutoDownload_vX.X.X_Portable.zip` — ZIP archive (for portable users)

## Steps for each release

```powershell
# 1. Bump version in AppVersion.cs and setup.iss
# 2. Publish
dotnet publish TelegramAutoDownload/TelegramAutoDownload.csproj -c Release -r win-x64 --self-contained true -p:PublishSingleFile=true -o publish/

# 3. Authenticode sign (REQUIRED for Smart App Control / SmartScreen — see scripts/sign-release.ps1)
$env:CODE_SIGN_PFX = "C:\path\to\cert.pfx"
$env:CODE_SIGN_PASSWORD = "..."
.\scripts\sign-release.ps1

# 4. Create ZIP (after signing so portable build is signed too)
Compress-Archive -Path publish/* -DestinationPath "TelegramAutoDownload_vX.X.X_Portable.zip" -Force

# 5. Compile installer (REQUIRED — never skip; /DSignRelease when cert env vars are set)
if ($env:CODE_SIGN_PFX) { & "C:\InnoSetup\ISCC.exe" /DSignRelease installer/setup.iss }
else { & "C:\InnoSetup\ISCC.exe" installer/setup.iss }

# 6. Release with BOTH files (never release with only one)
gh release create vX.X.X "TelegramAutoDownload_vX.X.X_Portable.zip" "TelegramAutoDownload_vX.X.X_Setup.exe" --title "vX.X.X" --notes "..."
```

## Code signing (Smart App Control)

Windows **Smart App Control** blocks unsigned apps with no verified publisher. Releases must be Authenticode-signed:

1. Obtain an **OV or EV** code signing certificate (e.g. Certum, Sectigo, DigiCert). EV builds reputation faster.
2. Set `CODE_SIGN_PFX` and `CODE_SIGN_PASSWORD` before `sign-release.ps1` and ISCC `/DSignRelease`.
3. Open-source projects can apply for free signing via [SignPath](https://signpath.io/).

## Never do

- ❌ Release with only ZIP and no Setup.exe
- ❌ Delete Setup.exe from a release to "fix" update issues — fix the code instead
- ❌ Skip the Inno Setup compile step
